  pub_how_eyebrow: 'How matching works',
  pub_how_title: 'Two sources of demand, one match',
  pub_how_body: 'Homatch compares what people want with what is on offer, using what they actually said: budget, district, type, size. It shows why it connected them, and never claims more than it knows.',
  pub_how_native_t: 'HOMATCH network',
  pub_how_native_d: 'People who state their own requirements on Homatch — in a Find Property search plan, a conversation or a viewing request.',
  pub_how_external_t: 'External sources',
  pub_how_external_d: 'Demand Homatch finds outside its own network, in sources it reads. Every signal is kept with a note of where it came from.',
  pub_how_match_t: 'A match, with its reasons',
  pub_how_match_d: 'When a requirement and a property line up, Homatch connects them, says why, and rates the fit in one of three words.',
  pub_how_decide_t: 'You decide',
