  /* ── VERIFY V6 STORY ── */
  verify_v6s_intro_title: 'What is the story of this project?',
  verify_v6s_intro_body: 'The story of this building does not begin with how it looks today. The official documents contain design materials and decisions from different periods that show how the project developed over the years.\nWe studied these materials to understand what was originally planned, what changed afterwards, which changes were approved and what we know about the building as it stands today.\nBelow we show everything in order, focusing on the points that truly matter before you buy an apartment.',
  verify_v6s_pending_title: 'Changes still under consideration',
  verify_v6s_pending_body: 'The official records show matters on which a final decision has not yet been confirmed. This in itself does not mean the project has a problem. Reviewing design changes during construction can be an ordinary procedure.\nWhat matters is understanding what exactly each change concerns and whether it could affect the building or your apartment.\nBelow we explain each matter separately and show the related official document.',
  verify_v6s_resolved_title: 'Recent changes: decided',
  verify_v6s_resolved_note: '{{count}} application(s) the city list still shows as under review were already decided: the published orders ({{dates}}) are described in the story above.',
  verify_v6s_steps_label: 'How the project evolved',
  verify_v6s_step_requested: 'What was requested',
  verify_v6s_step_changed: 'What changed in practice',
  verify_v6s_step_final: 'Is it final',
  verify_v6s_step_impact: 'What it means for a buyer',
  verify_v6s_step_unverified: 'What remains to verify',
  verify_v6s_status_approved: 'Approved',
  verify_v6s_status_permit: 'Permit issued',
  verify_v6s_status_corrected: 'Figures corrected',
  verify_v6s_status_returned: 'Returned',
  verify_v6s_status_under_review: 'Under review',
  verify_v6s_status_response_unread: 'Response published',
  verify_v6s_status_no_decision_read: 'No decision on record',
  verify_v6s_evidence: 'Documents and official records',
  verify_v6s_evidence_case: 'Case {{ref}}',
  verify_v6s_evidence_filed: 'filed {{date}}',
  verify_v6s_evidence_decision: 'decision No. {{number}}',
  verify_v6s_evidence_open_case: 'Open the case',
  verify_v6s_latest_title: 'Latest approved documentation',
  verify_v6s_status_title: 'Where the project stands today',
  verify_v6s_track_construction: 'Construction activity',
  verify_v6s_track_completion: 'Physical completion',
  verify_v6s_track_permit: 'Official approval',
  verify_v6s_track_commissioning: 'Commissioning',
  verify_v6s_tech_title: 'How well is the building planned?',
  verify_v6s_tech_body: 'Appearance is not all that matters when assessing a building. The structure, foundation, engineering systems, materials used and how thoroughly all of this is documented also deserve attention.\nOfficial drawings and technical documents show which solutions the project provided for. However, the quality described in a document and the work actually carried out are not the same thing.\nSo below we explain what the project provides for and what is worth checking in the building itself.',
  verify_v6s_materials_title: 'Materials and finishes',
  verify_v6s_materials_body: 'The materials named in the project documents help us understand what was planned. To judge their real condition, it is best to see the building in person.\nIt is advisable to check the details with the owner or, if the project has a sales representative, directly with them. Pay particular attention to the facade, windows, common areas, engineering systems and the condition in which the apartment is handed over.',
  verify_v6s_tech_term: 'What the term means',
  verify_v6s_tech_establishes: 'What the documents establish',
  verify_v6s_tech_why: 'Why it matters',
  verify_v6s_tech_cannot: 'What the documents cannot prove',
  verify_v6s_legal_title: 'What do we know about ownership and the legal position?',
  verify_v6s_legal_body: 'Before buying an apartment, three questions need answers: in whose name the property is registered, whether there are restrictions in force on it, and what state the building\'s official documentation is in.\nWe consider the records we found by their specific dates, because an old extract cannot always reflect the present situation.\nBelow you will see what is officially confirmed, what has changed over time and which information should be refreshed before the transaction.',
  verify_v6s_scope_unit: 'This apartment',
  verify_v6s_scope_parcel: 'Land parcel',
  verify_v6s_scope_building: 'Building',
  verify_v6s_scope_company: 'Developer',
  verify_v6s_scope_project: 'Project',
  verify_v6s_observed: 'Record date: {{date}}',
  verify_v6s_scale_title: 'How large is the project really?',
  verify_v6s_scale_body: 'The number of floors alone is not enough to understand a building\'s scale. It matters to know the land area, how much floor space may be built, and what share goes to residential, commercial or common areas.\nThese figures show the project\'s real size more clearly, and how space is distributed within the building.',
  verify_v6s_final_title: 'In the end, what do we think of this property?',
  verify_v6s_final_lede: 'After going through so much information, the main question is simple: how well founded is it to consider buying this property?\nWhat matters to us is not only what advantages the project has, but also how well those advantages are supported by documents and which questions remain to be verified.',
  verify_v6s_final_strengths: 'What the documents support',
  verify_v6s_final_concerns: 'What deserves attention, and why',
  verify_v6s_stance_positive: 'The evidence supports a positive assessment',
  verify_v6s_stance_balanced: 'The evidence supports a balanced assessment',
  verify_v6s_stance_cautious: 'The evidence calls for caution',
  verify_v6s_final_closing: 'Our aim is not to make the decision for you. We want you to make your choice as informed as possible, knowing the project\'s strengths and seeing in advance the matters worth extra attention.',

