  mortgage_rd_profile_title: 'What documents will I need?',
  mortgage_rd_profile_salaried: 'With a salary, banks usually ask for an employer letter and a bank statement. The longer you have worked in one place, the simpler it is.',
  mortgage_rd_profile_self_employed: 'Self-employed people can get a mortgage too. Instead of a salary certificate, the bank checks tax declarations, bank statements and client contracts. Steady, documented income is what matters.',
  mortgage_rd_profile_business_owner: 'For a business owner, the bank looks at the company accounts and at what you personally take out as dividends or salary.',
  mortgage_rd_profile_freelancer: 'For a freelancer, regular income visible on bank statements is key. Money from abroad counts too when documents prove it.',
  mortgage_rd_profile_rental: 'Rental income is checked with lease agreements, bank statements and tax declarations. Some banks count only part of the rent.',
  mortgage_rd_profile_emigrant: 'If you work abroad, banks consider your foreign income when documents and translations prove it. A loan in the currency you earn is safer.',
  mortgage_rd_profile_foreign_national: 'A foreign citizen can borrow from a Georgian bank, but the terms depend on the bank: some ask for a larger down payment or a residence permit.',
  mortgage_rd_learn_title: 'Explain it simply',
  mortgage_rd_x_co_q: 'What is a co-borrower?',
  mortgage_rd_x_co_a: 'A co-borrower takes the loan together with you. The bank counts their income too, but they are as responsible for repaying as you are, and their own loans count as well.',
  mortgage_rd_x_guarantor_q: 'Why would I need a guarantor?',
  mortgage_rd_x_guarantor_a: 'A guarantor does not take the loan, but promises the bank to pay if you cannot. Some banks ask for one when the income or history is short. For the guarantor it is a serious risk.',
  mortgage_rd_x_self_q: 'Can a self-employed person get a loan?',
  mortgage_rd_x_self_a: 'Yes. Instead of a salary certificate the bank checks declarations, statements and contracts. The longer and steadier the income history, the better.',
  mortgage_rd_x_valuation_q: 'Why does the bank ask for a property valuation?',
  mortgage_rd_x_valuation_a: 'The bank needs to know what the property securing the loan is worth. The loan is counted from that valuation, so if it comes in below the price you may need a larger down payment.',
