  mortgage_term_currency_risk_title: 'Currency risk',
  mortgage_term_nominal_rate_body: 'The nominal rate is the rate the bank charges interest at. It does not show every cost that comes with the loan.',
  mortgage_term_effective_rate_body: 'The effective rate gives a better picture of what the loan really costs. It includes the costs the law requires and when payments fall due. So when comparing two offers, do not rely on the nominal rate alone.',
  mortgage_term_fixed_rate_body: 'A fixed rate does not change for the agreed period. Always check whether it is fixed for the whole term or only for the first few years.',
  mortgage_term_variable_rate_body: 'A variable rate can change in the way the contract sets out. If it goes up, your monthly payment may go up too.',
  mortgage_term_reference_index_body: 'A variable rate is often made of two parts: a reference index and the bank\'s margin. When the index moves, your rate moves with it, while the margin usually stays the same.',
  mortgage_term_principal_body: 'The principal is the money you borrowed from the bank and have not yet paid back. Part of each monthly payment reduces the principal and part pays the interest.',
  mortgage_term_interest_payment_body: 'Interest is the price you pay the bank for using its money. It is worked out each month on the principal still owed, which is why early payments are mostly interest.',
  mortgage_term_monthly_installment_body: 'The monthly payment is what you pay the bank every month. It covers part of the principal and the interest, and sometimes a monthly fee and insurance too.',
  mortgage_term_amortization_body: 'This is a table showing what you pay each month, how much of it goes to interest and how much the remaining loan goes down.',
  mortgage_term_down_payment_body: 'The down payment is the part of the price you pay from your own money. The bigger it is, the less you borrow and the less interest builds up.',
  mortgage_term_pti_body: 'PTI shows what share of your income goes on monthly loan payments. The National Bank of Georgia caps this share so that repaying does not become too heavy.',
  mortgage_term_ltv_body: 'LTV shows what share of the property\'s value the loan covers. The National Bank caps this too, which is why a down payment is required.',
  mortgage_term_collateral_body: 'Collateral is property that secures the loan. With a mortgage it is usually the home you are buying. If the loan is not repaid, the bank can sell it.',
  mortgage_term_additional_collateral_body: 'Additional collateral is another property you offer the bank as security. It lowers the LTV, but it cannot make up for too little income: the monthly payment still has to be covered by what you earn.',
  mortgage_term_co_borrower_body: 'A co-borrower takes the loan with you and is equally responsible for repaying it. The bank counts their income too, so this often raises the amount you can borrow.',
  mortgage_term_guarantor_body: 'A guarantor does not take the loan but promises to pay if you cannot. A guarantor and a co-borrower are not the same thing: a guarantor\'s income usually does not raise how much you can repay.',
  mortgage_term_credit_history_body: 'Credit history is the record of how you repaid loans and cards in the past. Late payments are a risk signal for the bank, on-time payments help you.',
  mortgage_term_origination_fee_body: 'The origination fee is a one-time amount the bank charges for issuing the loan. It is often a percentage of the loan and it raises the effective rate.',
  mortgage_term_appraisal_body: 'The bank checks what the property used as security for the loan is worth. The value the bank accepts can differ from the asking price.',
  mortgage_term_insurance_body: 'Some mortgage products require property or other insurance. Check which insurance is needed, what it costs and whether it is included in the offer\'s figures.',
  mortgage_term_early_repayment_body: 'Early repayment means paying back part or all of the loan before the end of the term. It saves interest, but some banks charge a fee for it. Check your contract terms.',
  mortgage_term_refinancing_body: 'Refinancing means replacing your current loan with a new one. Sometimes it gives better terms, but before deciding compare every cost of the new and the old loan.',
  mortgage_term_total_repayment_body: 'Total repayment is everything you will pay the bank over the term: the principal, the interest and the known extra costs.',
  mortgage_term_total_cost_body: 'This is what you pay for servicing the loan and the related extra costs. A lower monthly payment does not always mean a lower total cost.',
  mortgage_term_currency_risk_body: 'If you earn in lari but repay the loan in a foreign currency, a change in the exchange rate can raise what you pay in lari.',
  mortgage_term_nominal_rate_example: 'At {{rate}} a year on a {{loan}} loan, the first month\'s interest is about {{interest}}.',
  mortgage_term_principal_example: 'On a {{loan}} loan, in the first month {{principal}} of the {{payment}} payment reduces the principal and {{interest}} goes to interest.',
  mortgage_term_interest_payment_example: 'On a {{loan}} loan at {{rate}}, the first month is {{interest}} of interest while the principal falls by only {{principal}}.',
  mortgage_term_monthly_installment_example: 'A {{loan}} loan at {{rate}} gives a monthly payment of {{payment}}: in the first month {{principal}} is principal and {{interest}} is interest.',
  mortgage_term_amortization_example: 'In the first month {{interest}} of the {{payment}} payment is interest, while in the last month the interest is only {{lastInterest}}, because little of the loan is left.',
  mortgage_term_effective_rate_example: 'On a {{loan}} loan with a {{feePct}} fee, that is {{fee}}, a nominal rate of {{rate}} works out at an effective rate of about {{effective}}. This is an estimate and does not replace the bank\'s official effective rate.',
  mortgage_term_origination_fee_example: 'On a {{loan}} loan a {{feePct}} fee is {{fee}}. You pay it once, but it raises the effective rate from {{rate}} to about {{effective}}.',
  mortgage_term_variable_rate_example: 'If the rate rises by 2 percentage points from {{rate}}, the payment on a {{loan}} loan goes from {{payment}} to about {{shocked}}.',
  mortgage_term_fixed_rate_example: 'At a fixed {{rate}} the payment is {{payment}} and does not change. If the same loan had a variable rate that rose by 2 percentage points, the payment would be about {{shocked}}.',
  mortgage_term_down_payment_example: 'On a {{price}} home, a {{down}} down payment is {{downPct}} of the price and the loan is {{loan}}.',
  mortgage_term_pti_example: 'If you earn {{income}} a month and the payment is {{payment}}, the PTI is about {{pti}}. Other loans push this share higher.',
  mortgage_term_ltv_example: 'A {{loan}} loan on a home worth {{price}} has an LTV of {{ltv}}.',
  mortgage_term_total_repayment_example: 'On a {{loan}} loan at {{rate}} over {{years}} years you repay about {{total}} in all, before extra costs.',
  mortgage_term_total_cost_example: 'On a {{loan}} loan at {{rate}} over {{years}} years the interest alone is about {{cost}}. Fees and insurance come on top.',
  mortgage_term_currency_risk_example: 'If the payment is {{payment}} and the exchange rate moves 10% against you, you will pay in lari what {{shocked}} costs today.',
  mortgage_term_info_aria: 'What it means: {{term}}',
